13. Public source, upstream submission and remote users.

No later than the first time you release, deliver to another party, or
deploy a modified version for operational use, publish its complete,
machine-readable Corresponding Source under this License. Each subsequent
modified version has the same obligation, including changes to a prior
fork. Operational use includes internal production, a private or public
network service, software as a service (SaaS), a hosted API and an
on-chain deployment. A downloadable
binary, container, patch or source-only release counts as delivery.
Private local development and testing under section 2 remains permitted.

Provide a stable, publicly accessible download for the exact revision,
without payment, registration, approval, a nondisclosure agreement or
recipient-specific credentials. A public repository with an accessible
immutable revision or versioned source archive suffices. A link to an
unmodified upstream release only suffices if it supplies the actual
Corresponding Source. Identify the relevant source revision with the
release, delivery or deployment. The source must be available throughout
the period you distribute or operate that version and for at least three
years after your last release, delivery or operational use of it. Any
longer obligation under section 6 continues to apply.

By the same release, delivery or deployment deadline, also submit the
exact modified revision to the original project identified by the Original
Project URL. Push the revision to a dedicated branch in that repository
if authorized, or open or update a pull request against that repository
from a branch containing the changes. Alternatively, publish the changes
on a dedicated branch of a public fork and submit the branch URL and
immutable commit ID to the original project's issue tracker. If that
repository cannot accept your pull request or issue, send the public
branch URL and immutable commit ID to info@gmwallet.app. Identify the
release or deployment and where its complete Corresponding Source can be
obtained. Keep the public source available for the period specified above.

Each distinct modified revision, including each SaaS update, must be
submitted. An existing branch or pull request may be updated to identify
successive revisions. Redeploying a previously submitted, identical
revision requires no duplicate submission. Submission is complete when
you have taken one of the steps above for the exact revision. GM Wallet
may merge, decline, close or leave it unreviewed. No acknowledgement or
merge is required, and closure does not require resubmission of the same
revision. Publication of source and submission upstream are separate
obligations. Section 18 governs express commercial exceptions.

Prominently offer all users interacting with a modified version remotely,
including users of a private service, free access to its Corresponding
Source. A visible Source link in the service or a documented, readily
discoverable source URL in its API or protocol documentation can do this.
For an on-chain deployment, publish the chain, address and revision with
the source link in the deployment record. These requirements also apply
when delivery or operation is delegated. Section 18 governs express
commercial exceptions.

You may combine independently licensed material only if you hold the
permissions needed from every relevant rightsholder and can comply with
all applicable terms. Separately distributed independent works keep their
own licenses. This custom license supplies no compatibility exception
on behalf of a third party.

