18. Group revenue and alternative commercial terms.

A company must obtain a separate paid written license from GM Wallet
before beginning or continuing licensed use if its annual group revenue
strictly exceeds USD 1,000,000. Exactly USD 1,000,000 remains eligible for
the community grant. The test applies to use for the company, including
through its employees, affiliates or contractors, whether internal,
hosted, customer-facing or otherwise. Each company relying on the grant
tests its own group. Merely obtaining or inspecting published source
under section 9 remains available to everyone.

Aggregate worldwide revenue from all business activities of the company
and entities that directly or indirectly control it, are controlled by it,
or are under common control with it, over the immediately preceding
twelve months. Control is the power to direct management or policies
through voting rights, contract or otherwise. Include each entity once
for its period of group membership. Eliminate intragroup transactions.
For a newly formed group use actual revenue since formation. Use revenue
recognized under applicable accounting standards before costs or expenses,
even if the company or group has a net loss. Count funds handled for
others only to the extent recognized as the group's own revenue. Convert
foreign currency at a consistently applied published rate applicable to
the period of recognition. On crossing the threshold, obtain the written
license before further licensed use.

